{"clock":1,"nonce":"7bd19c51189f40c0af77bba623c68ab8","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793906078,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:6229943402"},"data":{"body":"The actions from the related-work study ([docs/related-work.md](https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/blob/fix/lint-labels/docs/related-work.md), PR #99). The study compares git-board with git-issue, git-bug, Fossil, Radicle and the others. Each item below is small enough to become its own issue.\n\n**Forges and PMs**\n- [ ] A Forgejo/Gitea adapter that passes `forge/forgetest`, because \"any forge\" needs a forge a team can host itself.\n- [ ] Sync a GitHub Project item's position as a rank field, since that is how PMs keep priority.\n- [ ] A rank field on the web board: dragging a card sets it, and views sort by it. This gives rank to teams that left GitHub.\n- [ ] Map GitLab time tracking (`time_estimate`, `total_time_spent`) to fields, so GitLab users keep data they already record.\n\n**Ownership**\n- [ ] Sign entity commits with the person's SSH key, and mark authors who didn't sign. Owned data should say who wrote it, provably.\n- [ ] Optionally keep attachments in the datastore, and have export copy the files, so an export holds the whole issue.\n- [ ] A public \"new issue\" form on `git board serve`, off by default: a way in for people without a forge account.\n\n**Adoption**\n- [ ] Release archives and an install script that need neither `gh` nor a clone. Adoption starts with one command.\n- [ ] `git board import --git-issue \u003cdir\u003e`, since git-issue's users are the closest to ours.\n\n**Honesty and process**\n- [ ] Credit git-bug in ADR 0004 and the Storage spec: our data model comes from it.\n- [ ] Add a \"Prior art\" section to the PRD template, so looking for prior art becomes a habit.\n- [ ] Fix the drift that ADRs 0003, 0004 and 0007 list under \"Left open\". The spec is the contract.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_","title":"Related work: the study's 12 actions"}}]}